Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790265599999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790207999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The leg since bar 84 spends about 25 bars (87-111) inside a two-sided 2357.18-2680 band, so the leg is at least as range-like as trend-like and could be classified trading-range/channel rather than bull-trend.", "Momentum faded at the highs: bar 86 spiked to 2771 but closed 2515.3 with a long upper tail, and the 2643-2850 top area shows overlapping bars rather than clean trend bars.", "Bar 119 closes near its low (2684.16 in a 2641.37-2786.81 range) after a marginal new high 2850 versus the 2771 spike high, so an MTR from the high is not excluded.", "The first 84 bars of the window are bearish then rangebound, so the bull case rests only on roughly the last 36 bars."], "evidence_for": ["Higher swing lows dominate after bar 84: 2111 (bar 85 low), 2325.31 (bar 86 low), 2357.18 (bar 99 low), 2358.62 (bar 111 low), 2435.72 (bar 107 low).", "Higher swing highs over the same span: 2348.02 (bar 85), 2771 (bar 86), 2680 (bar 107), 2850 (bar 117).", "Bull bodies carry the advance: bar 84 opens 1916.51 and closes 2252.16, bar 107 opens 2437 and prints 2680, and bars 113-117 run from 2446.22 to a 2775.61 close.", "The current two-bar set-back (bars 118-119) is no deeper than the repeated pullbacks inside the 87-111 band, which is normal pullback behavior inside a bull leg."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Bars 0-10 form a bear leg: close slides from 2072.8 to 1568.55 and the window low 1368.42 is set on bar 10 (low 1368.42, close 1568.55).", "Bars 11-83 are a broad two-sided base bounded by low 1512.91 (bar 30) and high 1974.46 (bar 61); bars overlap heavily and every multi-bar swing is retraced.", "Bar 84 is a large bull breakout bar out of that base: open 1916.51, high 2293.8, low 1905.63, close 2252.16.", "Bar 85 closes 2326.32 (high 2348.02, low 2111); bar 86 spikes to 2771 but closes 2515.3, leaving a long upper tail.", "Bars 87-111 overlap in a 2357.18 (bar 99 low) to 2680 (bar 107 high) band, then bars 112-117 rally from 2358.62 to a new high 2850 (bar 117, close 2775.61).", "Bars 118-119 are consecutive bear bars; bar 119 opens 2752.43, trades 2641.37-2786.81 and closes 2684.16, in the lower part of its range and below bar 118's 2752.43 close."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Two-sided base after the opening bear leg: about 73 bars oscillating with heavy overlap between the 1512.91 low (bar 30) and the 1974.46 high (bar 61), with repeated failed pushes in both directions.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the base: bar 84 (open 1916.51, high 2293.8, close 2252.16) clears the base by a wide margin, bar 85 closes 2326.32, bar 86 spikes to 2771 and closes 2515.3. No exact horizontal boundary is claimed for this impulsive leg.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": null}, {"description": "Post-spike consolidation and channel-like portion of the bull leg: bars 87-111 overlap between low 2357.18 (bar 99) and high 2680 (bar 107) while keeping higher lows, so the leg is channel-like rather than a clean spike.", "end_time_ms": 1789516799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Two-bar bear reversal attempt at the bull high: bar 117 makes a new high 2850 and closes 2775.61, then bars 118-119 turn down and bar 119 closes 2684.16 near its low. Higher high over the 2771 spike high (bar 86) plus only two bear bars means this is a potential reversal pattern, not a confirmed reversal.", "end_time_ms": 1790207999999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2641.37", "start_time_ms": 1789948800000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation is supported if a bar closes above 2786.81 (bar 119 high) and then above 2850 (bar 117 high) with a strong bull body and little overlap.", "A close below 2641.37 (bar 119 low), then below 2435.72 (bar 107 low) and 2358.62 (bar 111 low), would break the sequence of higher lows and weaken the bull read.", "A close below 2325.31 (bar 86 low) would negate the post-base breakout structure and favor a major-trend-reversal or trading-range classification.", "If subsequent bars keep overlapping and closing mid-range around 2600-2800 for many sessions, the read shifts from bull-trend/channel toward trading-range/range."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "short", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": true, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790251199999, "directional_pressure": "bear", "evidence_against": ["The 2850 peak bar carries a 126.85 upper tail and closed ~4.5% below its high; the following ~16 bars have made no net upside progress, so the channel has stalled.", "A lower high at 2786.81 (bar 1790136000000) versus 2850, plus bar 1790164800000 breaking the 2716.01 low and closing near its low, forms a short-term lower-high/lower-low sequence.", "Six consecutive bars trade below the broken 2716.01 range low with no bull reversal bar, and the final bar closes in the lower quarter of its range, so the recent Always-In direction is short, not long.", "The current pullback (153.50 points) is about double the prior bull-channel pullback and retraces ~54% of the 2568.16-2850 leg, making the channel behave increasingly range-like.", "Upside probes have repeatedly attracted sellers with large tails: 2680 spike bar (1789128000000) and 2700-touch bars 1789804800000 and 1789948800000."], "evidence_for": ["Higher highs and higher lows from the 2358.62 window low to the 2850 high: successive swing lows 2486.12, 2568.16, then 2641.37/2633.31.", "The prior pullback (2643.52 to 2568.16) was contained and was followed by new highs (closes 2664.73, 2723.15, 2754.31, 2775.61), the pullback-then-continuation behavior of a bull channel.", "Buying appears at the lows of the break: bars 1790179200000 (close 2676.47, upper ~69% of range), 1790193600000 (2684.16, ~58%) and 1790222400000 (2692.23, ~80%) closed in the upper halves.", "The pullback has not closed below the 2568.16 prior bull-flag low, so the larger bull higher-low chain is technically unbroken.", "Final bar's low 2633.31 held above the 2608-2645 breakout zone and the bar closed back at 2647.90, above the 2645.88/2644.86 highs it briefly undercut."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Window 1788523200000-1790236800000 (120 H4 bars): open 2523.22, close 2647.90, window low 2358.62 (bar 1789488000000), window high 2850 (bar 1789977600000).", "Bar 1789977600000 (open 2658.81, high 2850, low 2658.06, close 2723.15) left a 126.85 upper tail and closed in the lower half of its 191.94-point range - a climax-form bar.", "Bars 1790020800000-1790150400000 overlap repeatedly inside 2716.01 (bar 1790049600000 low) to 2804.59 (bar 1790020800000 high) with two-sided closes: 2775.61, 2738.87, 2740.20, 2742.31, 2749.43, 2752.43, 2772.99, 2741.96, 2726.81.", "Bar 1790164800000 (open 2726.71, high 2727.77, low 2648.49, close 2659.00) is a 79.28-point bear bar closing in its lowest ~15%, breaking below the 2716.01 range low.", "Bars 1790179200000-1790222400000 hold entirely below 2716.01 (closes 2676.47, 2684.16, 2675.48, 2692.23) - a small flag under the broken range.", "Final bar 1790236800000 (open 2692.23, high 2693.42, low 2633.31, close 2647.90) makes a lower low below 2641.37 and closes in the lower quarter of its 60.11-point range.", "Bull higher-low chain from the window low: 2358.62 -> 2370.54 (1789574400000) -> 2486.12 (1789718400000) -> 2568.16 (1789891200000) -> 2641.37 (1790179200000) -> 2633.31 (1790236800000); the last link is only marginal and remains far above 2568.16.", "Current pullback 2786.81 (1790136000000 high) to 2633.31 = 153.50 points, about twice the prior bull-channel pullback 2643.52 (1789747200000 high) to 2568.16 (75.36 points), and retraces about 54% of the 2568.16-2850 leg.", "Bar 1790236800000 low 2633.31 dipped below the 2645.88/2644.86 highs of bars 1789920000000/1789934400000 but closed back at 2647.90 above them.", "Earlier window context: spike high 2680 (bar 1789128000000), a two-sided range 2464.27-2609.02 (bars 1789142400000-1789459200000), then a bear leg to 2358.62 before the bull leg."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Bull leg from the window low 2358.62 (bar 1789488000000) to the window high 2850 (bar 1789977600000), with rising swing lows 2486.12 and 2568.16 and mostly upper-half closes during the advance; dominant directional structure in the window.", "end_time_ms": 1789977600000, "kind": "swing", "lower_boundary": "2358.62", "start_time_ms": 1789488000000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}, {"description": "Mid-window two-sided range after the 2680 spike: repeated tests of both sides between 2464.27 and 2609.02 before the bear leg to 2358.62.", "end_time_ms": 1789459200000, "kind": "two-sided", "lower_boundary": "2464.27", "start_time_ms": 1789142400000, "upper_boundary": "2609.02"}, {"description": "Top consolidation after the climax: bars 1790020800000-1790150400000 overlap between 2716.01 and 2804.59 with two-sided closes; its 2716.01 low was broken by bar 1790164800000.", "end_time_ms": 1790150400000, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2716.01", "start_time_ms": 1790020800000, "upper_boundary": "2804.59"}, {"description": "Downside break of the top range: bar 1790164800000 breaks below 2716.01 and closes near its low; bars 1790179200000-1790222400000 hold below it, and bar 1790236800000 makes a lower low at 2633.31 with a close near its low. Pullback depth (153.50) is about twice the prior bull-channel pullback.", "end_time_ms": 1790236800000, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": "2633.31", "start_time_ms": 1790164800000, "upper_boundary": "2727.77"}, {"description": "Unconfirmed lower-high reversal candidate: bull climax at 2850 (bar 1789977600000), then a marginally lower high 2786.81 (bar 1790136000000) and loss of the 2716.01 range low. It lacks a lower low beneath the 2568.16 bull-flag low and any bear-trend follow-through, so it may still resolve as a bull pullback.", "end_time_ms": 1790236800000, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1789977600000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "H4", "transition_conditions": ["Bull resumption: a bull reversal bar or two closing back above 2716.01 and acceptance above 2748-2786 would read the drop as a bull-flag pullback and restore Always-In long.", "Bear continuation: consecutive closes below 2633.31 toward 2605.96/2586.68 would break the bull higher-low chain from 2568.16 and support the trading-range/possible-reversal read.", "Extended overlap between roughly 2633 and 2786 without new highs would firm the top structure into a trading range rather than a bull pullback, shifting the regime label toward trading-range.", "A re-test of 2850 that fails with a lower high versus a decisive close above 2786.81 would separate a double-top-like range from renewed channel continuation."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "stale"}}, "raw": {"H1": [{"close": "2648", "close_time_ms": 1789837199999, "high": "2649.83", "low": "2635.92", "open": "2640.01", "open_time_ms": 1789833600000, "volume": "1461504.185"}, {"close": "2645.08", "close_time_ms": 1789840799999, "high": "2658.79", "low": "2642.65", "open": "2648", "open_time_ms": 1789837200